{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-122876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/0abae6be42361d157d7cbd46f602d3a0d2044cfec551c61a2739ff9b56798cc3.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{13})=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =3\\cdot {m}_{11}+3\\cdot {m}_{12}+3\\cdot {m}_{13} \\\\  & =3({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] ["math" "3({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] ["math" "3\\cdot {m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{12}\\cdot {m}_{13}"] ["math" "3{m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/456aefd5e7fd85024c6d410d8b01bf3a49919504bb0023373bd0e94e768f584f.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{21}+1\\cdot {m}_{12}+2\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})"] ["math" "2{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/dca2037c7f7b5e45fca3268e4114dea0e939a6c08d02440fb1363f602f263273.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+4\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{31} \\\\  & =2{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/140