he volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{13})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{12}+2\\cdot {m}_{13} \\\\  & =2({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122877" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] ["math" "2\\cdot {m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{12}\\cdot {m}_{13}"] ["math" "2{m}_{11}-{m}_{12}-{m}_{13}"] ["math" "3({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122877" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/be2c8a433cbd5b812e8c02c5da6b8d2e713ffa8b21dfb327f553a09df8743a82.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+1\\cdot {m}_{21}+1\\cdot {m}_{12}+1\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})"] ["math" "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}-{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}-{m}_{12}-{m}_{22}"] ["math" "{m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{21}\\cdot {m}_{12}\\cdot {m}_{22}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122878" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5-x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=5-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=2 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=2 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=3+2+2+1=8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-75037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2,3,4},\\,{P}_{2}={1,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/48356d566752c064e9381c2f9ce27ef12bbdd86a29a2dab0d3dda05088630006.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{m}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}+2{m}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/90ed44b97d085413780f2dce297dd78ffa4c968a244e73c431d2e9aa30e14d22.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/860ba8cf7e5135f7e2eedcde7534fe9880feb38c29163625e32b79f18fce2f2f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,3)=2 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,3)=1 \\\\ {m}_{41} & =f(4,3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122961" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122961" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-work