 and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-2x-2y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/52c19da39a43cdbf1b1d2565669c391e59679b3bf9828f7c46755831b2b0890c.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/2acddf617eda8211e45d281329051f08a8b83788e24b70ebe8d526b58b195bba.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,3)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=5+3+3+1=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "87846dac51d25444c31204b9f6de804064097370d3684dc6c0562fb83ac14733"} {"question" "q-122965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/state.json" "file_sha256" "368fca94e02a20cb1673c4818aafc9ae1213e762579616e654fecac3250c2b75"} {"question" "q-122965" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen